[6.944, "o", "\u001b[7mpython cli.py --repo . --question \"how does --tunnel clean up the ngrok process \u001b[7mi\u001b[7mf the query fails?\" --tunnel\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[0.787, "o", "\u001b[A\u001b[7C\u001b[27mp\u001b[27my\u001b[27mt\u001b[27mh\u001b[27mo\u001b[27mn\u001b[27m \u001b[27mc\u001b[27ml\u001b[27mi\u001b[27m.\u001b[27mp\u001b[27my\u001b[27m \u001b[27m-\u001b[27m-\u001b[27mr\u001b[27me\u001b[27mp\u001b[27mo\u001b[27m \u001b[27m.\u001b[27m \u001b[27m-\u001b[27m-\u001b[27mq\u001b[27mu\u001b[27me\u001b[27ms\u001b[27mt\u001b[27mi\u001b[27mo\u001b[27mn\u001b[27m \u001b[27m\"\u001b[27mh\u001b[27mo\u001b[27mw\u001b[27m \u001b[27md\u001b[27mo\u001b[27me\u001b[27ms\u001b[27m \u001b[27m-\u001b[27m-\u001b[27mt\u001b[27mu\u001b[27mn\u001b[27mn\u001b[27me\u001b[27ml\u001b[27m \u001b[27mc\u001b[27ml\u001b[27me\u001b[27ma\u001b[27mn\u001b[27m \u001b[27mu\u001b[27mp\u001b[27m \u001b[27mt\u001b[27mh\u001b[27me\u001b[27m \u001b[27mn\u001b[27mg\u001b[27mr\u001b[27mo\u001b[27mk\u001b[27m \u001b[27mp\u001b[27mr\u001b[27mo\u001b[27mc\u001b[27me\u001b[27ms\u001b[27ms\u001b[27m i\u001b[27mf\u001b[27m \u001b[27mt\u001b[27mh\u001b[27me\u001b[27m \u001b[27mq\u001b[27mu\u001b[27me\u001b[27mr\u001b[27my\u001b[27m \u001b[27mf\u001b[27ma\u001b[27mi\u001b[27ml\u001b[27ms\u001b[27m?\u001b[27m\"\u001b[27m \u001b[27m-\u001b[27m-\u001b[27mt\u001b[27mu\u001b[27mn\u001b[27mn\u001b[27me\u001b[27ml\u001b[?2004l\r\r\n"]
[1.502, "o", "\u001b[33mngrok tunnel: https://jogger-botany-atrium.ngrok-free.dev/mcp/\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[19.367, "o", "WARNING:xai.attribution:Invalid citation range: cli.py:358-360 (file has 359 lines)\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\nNow let me look at the actual cli.py implementation.\r\n\r\n`--tunnel` cleans up ngrok using a `try/finally` block wrapped around the entire query-execution logic in `main()`.\r\n\r\nSpecifically:\r\n\r\n1. If `--tunnel` is passed, `_start_ngrok_tunnel(port)` is called to start the tunnel and get the public URL (\u001b[36m\u001b[1m`cli.py:284-287`\u001b[0m).\r\n2. All of the actual query logic — `--stability`, `--interactive` mode, and the normal single-question path — is executed inside a `try:` block (\u001b[36m\u001b[1m`cli.py:300-359`\u001b[0m).\r\n3. Regardless of whether that block completes normally or raises an exception (e.g., the query call fails, `run_query` throws, or any other error inside the `try`), the `finally` clause always runs:\r\n   ```python\r\n   finally:\r\n       if use_tunnel:\r\n           _stop_ngrok_tunnel()\r\n   ```\r\n   (\u001b[36m\u001b[1m`cli.py:358-360`\u001b[0m)\r\n4. `_stop_ngrok_tunnel()` itself just imports `pyngrok.ngrok` and calls `ngrok.kill()`, which terminates the ngrok process (\u001b[36m\u001b[1m`cli.py:78-81`\u001b[0m).\r\n\r\nSo even if `run_query"]
[0.000, "o", "`/`_answer_question` (or the stability/interactive loops) raise, Python's `finally` guarantees `_stop_ngrok_tunnel()` — and thus `ngrok.kill()` — still executes before `main()` returns, preventing an orphaned ngrok process. This matches the test name found in the pytest cache, `test_cli_tunnel_stopped_even_when_query_raises` (`.pytest_cache/v/cache/nodeids:39`), which exercises exactly this behavior, though I did not read that test file directly.\r\n\u001b[31m  [WARNING] INVALID_RANGE: cli.py:358-360\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nConfidence: HIGH  (none)\r\n\r\nFiles read: 1 of 51 total (1.96%)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  — cli.py: To find how --tunnel is implemented and how ngrok is started/stopped in cli.py, the CLI entry point of the repo.\r\n"]
